          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            The concept of
            %em state on a star-algebra
            is the formalization of the general idea of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/states"} states
            from the point of view of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+probability+theory"} quantum probability theory
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AQFT"} algebraic quantum theory
          %p
            In order to motivate the definition from more traditional formulations in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/state"} state
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle - \rangle
            is the information that allows to assign to each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observable"} observable
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/expectation+value"} expectation value
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle A\rangle
            that this observable has when the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physical+system"} physical system
            is assumed to be in that state.
          %p
            Often this is formalized in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schr%C3%B6dinger+picture"} Schrödinger picture
            where a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+states"} space of states
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℋ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}
            is taken as primary, and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observables"} observables
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation"} represented
            as suitable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+operators"} linear operators
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℋ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℋ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi \in \mathcal{H}
            a state (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pure+state"}> pure state
            ) the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/expectation+value"} expectation value
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            in this state is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+product"} inner product
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle \psi \vert A \vert \psi \rangle \coloneqq (\psi, A \psi)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+function"} linear function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\langle \psi \vert - \vert \psi \rangle
                  \\;\colon\;
                  \\mathcal{A}
                  \\longrightarrow
                  \\mathbb{C}
          %p
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+observables"} algebra of observables
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
          %p
            Conversely, in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisenberg+picture"} Heisenberg picture
            one may take the “abstract”
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+quantum+observables"} of observables
            as primary (i.e. not necessarily manifested as an
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operator+algebra"} operator algebra
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\langle - \rangle
                  \\;\colon\;
                  \\mathcal{A}
                  \\longrightarrow
                  \\mathbb{C}
          %p
            which is
            %em positive
            in that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle A^\ast A\rangle \geq 0
            and
            %em normalized
            in that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle 1\rangle = 1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+states"} space of states
            may be (re-)constructed from this
            %em a posteriori
            via the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GNS+construction"} GNS construction
          %p
            Traditionally this definition is considered for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras+of+observables"} algebras of observables
            which are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2A-algebras"} C*-algebras
            (as usually required for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} non-perturbative quantum field theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Fredenhagen03"} Fredenhagen (2003) Sec. 2
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#Landsman17"} Landsman (2017) Def. 2.4
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star-algebras"} star-algebras
            (
            %a{:href => "#Meyer95"}> Meyer (1995), I.1.1
            ), such as for instance for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+power+series+algebras"} formal power series algebras
            that appear in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative quantum field theory
            (e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BordemannWaldmann96"} Bordemann-Waldmann (1996) Def. 1
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#FredenhagenRejzner12"} Fredenhagen &amp; Rejzner (2012) Def. 2.4
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#KhavkineMoretti15"} Khavkine &amp; Moretti (2015) Def. 6
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Duetsch18"} Dütsch (2018) Def. 2.11
          %p#AsPositiveLinearFunctionals
            Of course, the notion of states depends only on the
            = succeed "-algebra\u2019s" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+order"} partially ordered
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+space"} complex vector space
            (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "C-star-algebra#PartialOrderAndPositiveElements"} here
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+order"} partially ordered
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            %em positive linear functionals
            or similar (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Murphy90"} Murphy (1990) §3.3
          %p
            The perspective that states are normalized positive linear functionals on the algebra of observables is implicit in traditional
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative quantum field theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-point+function"} 2-point function
            corresponding to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum+state"} vacuum state
            or more generally a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-free+quantum+state"} quasi-free quantum state
            (the
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hadamard+propagator"} Hadamard propagator
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+quantum+field+theory"} algebraic quantum field theory
            (see e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Fredenhagen03"} Fredenhagen 03, section 2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star-algebras"} star-algebras
            of observables that are not necessarily
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2A-algebras"} C*-algebras
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+algebraic+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative algebraic quantum field theory
            (e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BordemannWaldmann96"} Bordemann-Waldmann 96
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#FredenhagenRejzner12"} Fredenhagen-Rejzner 12, def. 2.4
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#KhavkineMoretti15"} Khavkine-Moretti 15, def. 6
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Duetsch18"} Dütsch 18, def. 2.11
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#DefinitionForUnitalStarAlgebras For unital star algebras
          #StateOnAStarAlgebra.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/state"} state
                on a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unital+algebra"} unital
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star+algebra"} star algebra
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unital"} unital
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star-algebra"} star-algebra
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℂ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
              %em state
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+function"} linear function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\rho \;\colon\; \mathcal{A} \longrightarrow \mathbb{C}
            %p such that
            %ol
              %li#PositivityCondition
                %p
                  (positivity) for all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒜
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \mathcal{A}
                  the value of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ρ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
                  on the product
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi A
                          %mo *
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^\ast A
                  is
                %ol
                  %li
                    %p
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+part"} real
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mi ρ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi A
                              %mo *
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mo ↪
                            %mi ℂ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,\rho(A^\ast A) \in \mathbb{R} \hookrightarrow \mathbb{C}
                  %li
                    %p
                      as such
                      = succeed ":" do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-negative+real+number"} non-negative
                #eq:Positivity.maruku-equation
                  %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ρ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi A
                          %mo *
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\rho(A^\ast A) \geq 0
              %li
                %p (normalization)
                #eq:Normalization.maruku-equation
                  %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ρ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\rho(\mathbf{1}) = 1
                %p
                  for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒜
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{1} \in \mathcal{A}
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit"} unit
                  in the algebra.
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Meyer95"} Meyer 95, I.1.1
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BordemannWaldmann96"} Bordemann-Waldmann 96
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#FredenhagenRejzner12"} Fredenhagen-Rejzner 12, def. 2.4
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#KhavkineMoretti15"} Khavkine-Moretti 15, def. 6
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Landsman17"} Landsman 2017, Def. 2.4
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+theory"} probability theoretic
                interpretation of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/state+on+a+star-algebra"} state on a star-algebra
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star+algebra"} star algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              equipped with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/state+on+a+star-algebra"} state
              is also called a
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+probability+space"} quantum probability space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              is in fact a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/von+Neumann+algebra"} von Neumann algebra
          #StatesFormAConvexSet.num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/state+on+a+star-algebra"} states
                form a
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convex+set"} convex set
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              a unital
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star-algebra"} star-algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              of states on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              according to def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StateOnAStarAlgebra"}
              is naturally a
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convex+set"} convex set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ρ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ρ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho_1, \rho_2 \colon \mathcal{A} \to \mathbb{C}
              two states then for every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \in [0,1] \subset \mathbb{R}
              also the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+combination"} linear combination
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝒜
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mi p
                                %msub
                                  %mi ρ
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo +
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mn 1
                                %mo −
                                %mi p
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %msub
                                  %mi ρ
                                  %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℂ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %mi p
                            %msub
                              %mi ρ
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo +
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo −
                            %mi p
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msub
                              %mi ρ
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathcal{A}
                    \&amp;\overset{p \rho_1 + (1-p) \rho_2}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\mathbb{C}
                    \\\
                    A &amp;\mapsto&amp; p \rho_1(A) + (1-p) \rho_2(A)
                    }
            %p is a state.
          #PureStateOnAStarAlgebra.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pure+state"}> pure state
                )
            %p
              A state
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho \colon \mathcal{A} \to \mathbb{C}
              on a unital
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star-algebra"} star-algebra
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StateOnAStarAlgebra"}
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pure+state"} pure state
              if it is extremal in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convex+set"} convex set
              of all states (remark
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StatesFormAConvexSet"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo =
                    %mi p
                    %msub
                      %mi ρ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo −
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi ρ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\rho = p \rho_1 + (1-p) \rho_2
            %p
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \in (0,1)
              implies that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ρ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi ρ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho_1 = \rho_2
              (hence
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo =
                      %mi ρ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} = \rho
          %h3#for_algebras
            For
            = succeed "-Algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
          %p
            The following discusses states specifically on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2A-algebras"} C*-algebras
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              An element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              of an (abstract)
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^*
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+operator"} positive
              if it is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-adjoint+operator"} self-adjoint
              and its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+of+an+operator"} spectrum
              is contained in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0, \infinity)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \ge 0
              and say that the set of all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+operators"} positive operators
              is the positive cone (of a given
              = succeed "-algebra)." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^*
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              This definition is motivated by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
              situation, where an operator
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℬ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \mathcal{B} (\mathcal{H})
              is called
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+operator"} positive
              if for every vector
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℋ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in \mathcal{H}
              the inequality
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle x, A x \rangle \ge 0
              holds. If the abstract
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^*
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functional+calculus"} functional calculus
              we can define a self adjoint operator
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \coloneqq f(A)
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi t
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(t) := t^{1/2}
              and get
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mi B
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle x, A x \rangle = \langle B x, B x \rangle \ge 0
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+functional"} linear functional
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
              on an
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^*
              %strong positive
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \ge 0
              implies that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho(A) \ge 0
            %p
              A
              %strong state
              of a unital
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^*
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+functional"} linear functional
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
              is positive and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho(1) = 1
          %p
            Though the mathematical notion of state is already close to what physicists have in mind, they usually restrict the set of states further and consider normal states only. We let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℛ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{R}
            be an
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^*
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
            an representation of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℛ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{R}
            on a Hilbert space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℋ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}
          .num_theorem
            %h6#definitiontheorem Definition/Theorem
            %p
              A
              %strong normal state
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
              is a state that satisfies one of the following equivalent conditions:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ρ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
                  is weak-operator continuous on the unit ball of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ℛ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi(\mathcal{R})
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ρ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
                  is strong-operator continuous on the unit ball
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ℛ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi(\mathcal{R})
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ρ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
                  is ultra-weak continuous.
              %li
                %p
                  There is an operator
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trace+class"} trace class
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℋ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}
                  with
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi tr
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tr(A) = 1
                  such that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ρ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi π
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi tr
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mi π
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho(\pi(R)) = tr(A \pi(R))
                  for all
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi R
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi ℛ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \in \mathcal{R}
          %p
            This appears as
            %a{:href => "#KadisonRingrose"} KadisonRingrose, def. 7.1.11, theorem 7.1.12
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p This list is not complete, there are more commonly used equivalent characterizations of normal states.
            %p
              The last one is most frequently used by physicists, in that context the operator
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is also called a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/density+matrix"} density matrix
              or density operator.
          %p
            Sometimes the observables of a system are described by an abstract
            = succeed "-algebra," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^*
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong folium
              of a representation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
              of an
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^*
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℛ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{R}
              on a Hilbert space is the set of normal states of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi π
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℛ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi(\mathcal{R})
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_7 Definition
            %p
              A state
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
              of a representation is called a
              %strong vector state
              if there is a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℋ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in \mathcal{H}
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho(\pi(R)) = \langle \pi(R)x, x \rangle
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℛ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \in \mathcal{R}
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              Normal states are vector states if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℛ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{R}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/von+Neumann+algebra"} von Neumann algebra
              with a separating vector. More precisely: Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℛ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{R}
              be a von Neumman algebra acting on a Hilbert space
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℋ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
              be a normal state of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℛ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{R}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℋ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in \mathcal{H}
              be a separating vector for
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℛ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{R}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℋ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in \mathcal{H}
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi Ry
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho(R) = \langle Ry, y \rangle
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℛ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \in \mathcal{R}
          %p
            This appears as
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#KadisonRingrose"} KadisonRingrose, theorem 7.2.3
          %p
            The set of states of an
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^*
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+quantum+states"} state space
          %p
            The state space is non-empty (define a state on the subalgebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C} 1
            and extend it to the whole
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^*
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hahn-Banach+theorem"} Hahn-Banach theorem
            = succeed "-compact," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ^*
            %span.newWikiWord
              Krein-Milman theorem
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Krein-Milman+theorem"} ?
            (see Wikipedia:
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Krein%E2%80%93Milman_theorem"} Krein-Milman theorem
            = succeed "-closure" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ^*
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_8 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong pure state
              is a state that is an extreme point of the state space.
          %p
            The term “pure” originates from the notion of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entanglement"} entanglement
          %h2#Examples Examples
          %p
          #ClassicalProbabilityMeasureAsStateOnMeasurableFunctions.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (classical
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+measure"} probability measure
                as state on
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+functions"} measurable functions
              %br/
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+space"} locally compact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff space
              equipped with a compatible structure of a classical
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+space"} probability space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure+space"} measure space
              which normalized total measure
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∫
                        %mi Ω
                      %mi d
                      %mi μ
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int_\Omega d\mu = 1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A} \coloneqq C_0(\Omega)
              be the algebra of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
              with values in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vanishing+at+infinity"} vanishing at infinity
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star+algebra"} star algebra
              by pointwise
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+conjugation"} complex conjugation
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/expectation+value"} expectation value
              with respect to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
              defines a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/state+on+a+star-algebra"} state
              (def.
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StateOnAStarAlgebra"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Ω
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %msub
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                                  %mi μ
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℂ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ∫
                              %mi Ω
                            %mi A
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mi d
